  "goodToKnow": "Die Eiche is an oak: eine alte Eiche, Möbel aus Eiche. The oak was a German national symbol in the 19th century, and oak leaves appeared on the backs of the old Pfennig coins and still appear on German euro cents. Die Eichel is an acorn, and das Eichhörnchen (squirrel) is literally oak-little-horn. Was schert es eine deutsche Eiche, wenn sich eine Sau daran reibt? means why should an oak care if a pig rubs against it, a proverb about ignoring insults."
